--- body ---
## Problem

The v1 tag vocabulary hardcodes four values in Go source: needs-human,
deferred, post-talk, post-conference. The first two are generic workflow
states. The last two are personal calendar labels that leaked into a
reusable spec. No live ticket has ever used post-talk or post-conference.

Affected code:
- ergspecv1.go: validTagValues map (compile-time)
- ready.go: skipReadyTags map (duplicate, also compile-time)
- bootstrap_assets.go: AGENTS.md and spec-erg-v1.md mention the values
- validate_test.go: test fixtures reference post-talk/post-conference

## Design

Tag vocabulary comes from a configuration file `tickets/.erg-tags`,
one value per line. Lines starting with `#` are comments, blank lines
are ignored.

Default file created by `erg init`:

```
# Tag vocabulary for this project.
# One tag per line. Remove or add lines to fit your workflow.
# All tags suppress the ticket from `erg ready` output.
needs-human
deferred
```

### Lookup order

1. `$ERG_TICKET_DIR/.erg-tags` (or discovered ticket dir)
2. If missing, fall back to built-in defaults: needs-human, deferred

### Validator behavior

- If `.erg-tags` exists and is readable, its contents are the closed set.
- If `.erg-tags` is absent, fall back to built-in defaults.
- Empty `.erg-tags` (no non-comment lines) means no tags are valid.
- Unknown tag values still fail validation (closed-set contract preserved).

### erg ready behavior

All tags in the vocabulary suppress readiness (current behavior for
skipReadyTags). The two maps collapse into one: the vocabulary IS the
skip set.

## Actions

1. Add `.erg-tags` to initAssetPaths and bootstrap_assets.go
2. Add loadTagVocabulary(dir string) -> map[string]bool function
3. Replace validTagValues with runtime-loaded vocabulary in parseErgBytes
4. Replace skipReadyTags with same vocabulary in ready.go
5. Remove post-talk and post-conference from built-in defaults
6. Update spec-erg-v1.md: Tag values come from .erg-tags
7. Update AGENTS.md: mention .erg-tags
8. Update test fixtures

## Exit criteria

- [ ] `erg init` creates tickets/.erg-tags with needs-human and deferred
- [ ] Validator reads .erg-tags when present, falls back to defaults
- [ ] `erg ready` uses same vocabulary (one source of truth)
- [ ] post-talk and post-conference removed from defaults
- [ ] Existing tests updated, new tests cover: custom .erg-tags,
      missing .erg-tags fallback, empty .erg-tags
- [ ] `make check` passes
